BPAYÂ® out available up to the available balance of your account.","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-access-and-payment-methods"},{"featureType":"OTHER","additionalInfo":"Construction Loans. Borrowers can draw down their home loan in stages to fund their renovation or new home build."},{"featureType":"OTHER","additionalInfo":"Repayments can be made via Direct Debit or Salary Credit/Electronic Funds Transfer."},{"featureType":"REDRAW","additionalInfo":"Access additional payments you've made through the redraw facility. Redraw cannot be accessed on fixed rate loan accounts until after the fixed period expires.","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-repayment-and-redraw-options"},{"featureType":"OTHER","additionalInfo":"Maximum Loan term of up to 30 years.","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-loan-limits"},{"featureType":"OTHER","additionalInfo":"Minimum increase amount $25,000.","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-loan-limits"},{"featureType":"EXTRA_REPAYMENTS","additionalInfo":"Extra repayments can be made in addition to regular monthly loan repayments. Note: You can make extra repayments on your fixed home loan of up to $10,000 per account which can be made each year without penalty (additional payments above this amount may incur break costs). The 12-month period is calculated from the date the fixed term commenced.","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/compare-home-loans.html#tab-panels-0-access-and-payment-methods"},{"featureType":"GUARANTOR","additionalInfo":"Subject to review, a guarantor can be nominated during the loan origination process."}],"fees":[{"name":"Construction Administration Fee","feeType":"EVENT","feeMethodUType":"fixedAmount","additionalInfo":"A one-off fee payable at settlement which covers valuation costs and progress payments during construction period.","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/assets/bfs/documents/personal-direct/home-loans/home-loans-product-guide.pdf","currency":"AUD","fixedAmount":{"amount":"1500.00"}},{"name":"Application Fee","feeType":"UPFRONT","feeMethodUType":"fixedAmount","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-ongoing-account-fees","currency":"AUD","fixedAmount":{"amount":"0.00"}},{"name":"Monthly Fee","feeType":"PERIODIC","feeMethodUType":"fixedAmount","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-ongoing-account-fees","additionalValue":"P1M","currency":"AUD","fixedAmount":{"amount":"0.00"}},{"name":"Annual Package Fee","feeType":"PERIODIC","feeMethodUType":"fixedAmount","additionalInfo":"$124 charged every 6 months in arrears based on loan Settlement Date. One package fee covers up to 5 loan applications that are submitted within 6 months, and where borrowers are common across each of the applications","additionalInfoUri":"https://www.macquarie.com.au/home-loans/offset-home-loan.html#tab-panels-0-ongoing-account-fees","additionalValue":"P1Y","currency":"AUD","fixedAmount":{"amount":"248.00"}},{"name":"Break Cost","feeType":"OTHER","feeMethodUType":"variable","additionalInfo":"Break costs may be payable on early repayment during fixed rate periods if any of the following three events occur: 1. The whole of a fixed rate Loan Account is repaid. 2. The borrower makes additional repayments in excess of $10,000 into a fixed rate Loan Account in any year of the fixed rate term (i.e. in any 12 months from the date the fixed rate period commences). 3. The borrower changes the whole or part of the fixed rate Loan Account to another type of interest rate or repayment type, including changing to a different fixed rate period. The break cost could be substantial. Contact us for further information.","additionalInfo